WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.082 --> 00:00:17.925
deserve a treat after all that shopping," Cecil said, pausing in front of a smoothie store.

2
00:00:18.926 --> 00:00:19.786
Mia laughed.

3
00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:24.068
"Buying new shoes isn't that hard."

4
00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:30.072
Suddenly they heard a commotion behind them, and a female voice yelled, "Help!"

5
00:00:31.436 --> 00:00:35.777
Cecil and Mia turned around and saw a man lying on the ground.

6
00:00:35.797 --> 00:00:38.118
"My husband collapsed!"

7
00:00:38.478 --> 00:00:39.458
the woman cried.

8
00:00:39.478 --> 00:00:44.220
"I'll dial 9-1-1," Cecil said, pulling out his phone.

9
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.181
The woman dropped to her knees beside her husband.

10
00:00:48.201 --> 00:00:51.262
"He's not breathing!"

11
00:00:52.122 --> 00:00:56.503
People gathered around, looking worried, but no one moved to help.

12
00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:59.624
"This is 9-1-1," the operator said.

13
00:01:00.364 --> 00:01:01.405
"What is your emergency?"

14
00:01:02.385 --> 00:01:08.808
Cecil told the operator his name and location and explained the situation before passing his phone to the

15
00:01:08.908 --> 00:01:12.249
woman. "I'm Stephanie Hart," she said.

16
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:16.111
She answered a few questions, then her eyes went wide.

17
00:01:16.131 --> 00:01:19.633
"I don't know how to do CPR, but I'll try!"

18
00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:24.375
Cecil put his phone on speaker mode so Mrs.

19
00:01:24.455 --> 00:01:26.696
Hart could hear the operator's instructions.

20
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.682
Mrs. Hart put her hands on her husband's chest and began to press.

21
00:01:32.822 --> 00:01:36.424
Soon an ambulance arrived and paramedics jumped out.

22
00:01:37.384 --> 00:01:39.065
One of them quickly checked Mr.

23
00:01:39.105 --> 00:01:42.006
Hart before taking over CPR from Mrs.

24
00:01:42.046 --> 00:01:48.249
Hart. Within seconds the man was breathing, and the paramedics put him in the ambulance.

25
00:01:48.269 --> 00:01:53.231
"That was awful," Mia said.

26
00:01:54.032 --> 00:01:54.812
Cecil nodded.

27
00:01:57.264 --> 00:02:01.186
That evening Cecil recounted the frightening episode to his family.

28
00:02:01.206 --> 00:02:05.207
"You did the right thing by calling 9-1-1," Dad said.

29
00:02:05.227 --> 00:02:08.749
"I wanted to do more," Cecil said.

30
00:02:08.769 --> 00:02:15.011
"I've seen two-hour CPR courses with certified instructors at the community college," Dad said.

31
00:02:15.992 --> 00:02:16.912
Cecil smiled.

32
00:02:16.932 --> 00:02:18.473
"Let's sign up!"

33
00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:23.755
Two weeks later Cecil and Dad attended the class.

34
00:02:24.635 --> 00:02:28.929
Miss Reese, the instructor, stood behind a desk in front of the room.

35
00:02:29.729 --> 00:02:33.830
A training dummy of a man's head and torso was propped against the desk.

36
00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:38.031
"CPR saves lives," she began.

37
00:02:38.051 --> 00:02:45.333
"When the heart stops due to something like a heart attack or near drowning, blood circulation stops too.

38
00:02:46.274 --> 00:02:49.494
It only takes minutes for brain damage to occur.

39
00:02:50.455 --> 00:02:54.376
CPR keeps blood flowing to the brain to help prevent damage.

40
00:02:55.296 --> 00:02:58.999
We'll start by learning how to perform CPR on an adult.

41
00:02:59.699 --> 00:03:01.481
Does anyone know what to do first?"

42
00:03:02.721 --> 00:03:06.144
Cecil half-raised his hand, and Miss Reese called on him.

43
00:03:06.164 --> 00:03:08.326
"Call 9-1-1?"

44
00:03:08.706 --> 00:03:09.847
he said hesitantly.

45
00:03:09.867 --> 00:03:11.568
"That's right!"

46
00:03:11.888 --> 00:03:13.209
the instructor said.

47
00:03:13.229 --> 00:03:16.451
"Why don't you come up and help me demonstrate?"

48
00:03:17.392 --> 00:03:22.536
Dad gave Cecil an encouraging smile, and Cecil made his way to the front of the classroom.

49
00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.761
Miss Reese placed the dummy on the floor.

50
00:03:25.781 --> 00:03:30.143
"First check whether Darrell the Dummy is conscious."

51
00:03:31.283 --> 00:03:33.124
Cecil knelt beside the dummy.

52
00:03:34.165 --> 00:03:35.485
"Umm, Darrell?

53
00:03:36.006 --> 00:03:36.646
Can you hear me?"

54
00:03:37.286 --> 00:03:40.028
"Darrell's not responsive," Miss Reese said.

55
00:03:40.048 --> 00:03:43.889
"He's definitely unconscious," Cecil agreed.

56
00:03:43.909 --> 00:03:49.232
"Next," Miss Reese said, "check if Darrell is breathing."

57
00:03:50.088 --> 00:03:54.350
She showed Cecil how to put his ear near Darrell's mouth and nose to listen for breathing.

58
00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:59.492
"He's not breathing," Cecil said.

59
00:03:59.512 --> 00:04:07.175
"Since Darrell is unconscious and not breathing, that means we should perform CPR," Miss Reese said.

60
00:04:07.195 --> 00:04:13.078
"He needs to be on his back on a firm surface, and luckily he already is.

61
00:04:14.038 --> 00:04:18.320
Before starting CPR though, we need to make sure his airway is clear.

62
00:04:19.264 --> 00:04:23.186
We can't perform CPR if Darrell's airway is obstructed.

63
00:04:24.106 --> 00:04:26.327
Tilt the head back and lift the chin.

64
00:04:27.047 --> 00:04:31.909
Then check inside Darrell's mouth for anything that might cause him to choke."

65
00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.771
Cecil did as Miss Reese told him.

66
00:04:34.791 --> 00:04:36.171
"It's clear."

67
00:04:36.191 --> 00:04:40.893
"Now we can start chest compressions," Miss Reese said.

68
00:04:41.894 --> 00:04:46.976
Following Miss Reese's instructions, Cecil put a hand in the center of the dummy's chest.

69
00:04:47.692 --> 00:04:50.013
He placed his other hand on top of the first.

70
00:04:50.653 --> 00:04:54.495
With his elbows stiff, he pushed down on the dummy's chest.

71
00:04:54.515 --> 00:04:57.696
"A little harder," Miss Reese said.

72
00:04:57.716 --> 00:05:02.758
"Push five to six centimeters—about a third of the depth of the chest.

73
00:05:03.578 --> 00:05:12.702
Keep going at about 100 to 120 compressions per minute until the person begins breathing or help arrives."

74
00:05:13.702 --> 00:05:17.204
Cecil pushed and pushed—it was hard work!

75
00:05:18.656 --> 00:05:20.077
"He's breathing!"

76
00:05:20.578 --> 00:05:23.440
Miss Reese announced to applause from the class.

77
00:05:24.201 --> 00:05:27.523
Dad and the other members of the class took turns saving Darrell.

78
00:05:28.364 --> 00:05:33.328
Cecil even tried another rescue himself, feeling more confident the second time.

79
00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:40.674
After class Cecil and Dad met Mia at the smoothie store and told her about what they had

80
00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:48.593
learned. "It's scary to think that any one of these people could collapse," Mia said, looking out the

81
00:05:48.673 --> 00:05:49.494
store windows.

82
00:05:49.514 --> 00:05:52.898
"It's very unlikely," Dad said.

83
00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:58.665
"I hope I never have to use CPR, but I feel better now that I know what to

84
00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.186
do," Cecil said.

85
00:06:00.206 --> 00:06:02.909
"Maybe you could take the class too."

86
00:06:03.931 --> 00:06:04.832
Mia smiled.

87
00:06:04.852 --> 00:06:06.994
"I'm going to sign up!"
